---
title: Draw Promotions
description: Collect entries from members and draw winners for a limited pool of prizes.
nav:
  title: Draws
  path: Digital Assets/Loyalty Programs
  order: 3
---
A draw rewards a limited number of members chosen at random, rather than everyone who qualifies.

Members earn entries by generating qualifying Events. When the Promotion ends, Centrapay picks winners from those entries, issues the prizes, and closes the Promotion.

## How a Draw Differs

| | Challenge | Draw |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `endsAt` | Optional | Required - it is when the draw runs |
| `params.target` | Required | Not allowed |
| `params.progress` | Not allowed | Required |
| `repeatable` | Allowed | Not allowed |
| Reward supply | Optional | Required on every reward |

## Earning Entries

A draw has no target. Instead, `params.progress` sets the bounds on how many entries a single Account can earn.

{% properties %}
  {% property name="minimum" type="number" required=true %}
    The progress an Account must reach before it starts earning entries. The qualifying Event that takes the Account to `minimum` earns its first entry, and every qualifying Event after that earns another.
  {% /property %}

  {% property name="maximum" type="number" %}
    The most progress a single Account can accumulate. Once reached, the Account stops earning entries. Leave it out for an uncapped draw.
  {% /property %}
{% /properties %}

More entries mean better odds: an Account that earns six entries has six chances of being picked, but can still only win once.

## Prizes

A draw's rewards describe prize tiers rather than a single payout, so `params.rewards` is an `or` group. Each direct child of that `or` is a separate prize that is drawn for on its own.

Every prize must declare a `totalSupply`, and that is what sets how many winners it has. Multiply `amount` by the number of winners you want: a prize of `amount` 1000 awarded to ten members needs a `totalSupply` of 10000.

```json {% title="One grand prize, then ten runner-up prizes" %}
{
  "type": "draw",
  "eventType": "payment-request:paid",
  "endsAt": "2026-03-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "params": {
    "progress": {
      "minimum": 5
    },
    "rewards": {
      "or": [
        { "assetType": "centrapay.nzd.main", "amount": "10000", "totalSupply": "10000" },
        { "assetType": "centrapay.nzd.main", "amount": "1000", "totalSupply": "10000" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

The example above enters an Account after five qualifying payments, and offers one grand prize of $100, then ten runner-up prizes of $10 each.

## Running the Draw

The draw runs when `endsAt` passes. No API call is needed.

Winners are drawn one prize at a time, each from the whole pool of entries. An Account can win at most once across the entire draw, so once it is picked its remaining entries are set aside. If a prize has more winners than there are eligible entries, the leftover prizes go unclaimed.

Each reward on the Promotion then carries an `issuedToAccountIds` array naming its winners; an empty array means nobody won that prize.

Once prizes are issued the Promotion is ended, completing the winners' memberships and expiring everyone else's.
